Configuring Alerts with PagerDuty
Step 1: Log in to PagerDuty
Go to the PagerDuty website: https://www.pagerduty.com/.
Log in to your PagerDuty account using your credentials.
Step 2: Create a New Service (If needed)
If you don’t have a service already set up in PagerDuty, follow these steps to create one:

Press enter or click to view image in full size

Services Page in Pager Duty.

In PagerDuty, navigate to the Services tab.
Click + New Service.
Enter the required details for the service (e.g., service name).
Press enter or click to view image in full size

4. Under Integration Type, choose Events API v2 (this is the integration type you’ll use to send alerts from Grafana).

5. Click Add Service.

Step 3: Obtain the Integration Key
After creating the service, you will be directed to the service’s Configuration page.
Scroll down to the Integrations section.
Press enter or click to view image in full size

Integration Settings on Pagerduty

3. Under Integration Settings, you will see the Integration Key.

This key is unique to the service you just created and will be used in Grafana to send alerts to PagerDuty.
Copy the Integration Key provided.
Step 5: Use the Integration Key in Grafana
Now that you have the integration key, go back to Grafana and use it to set up the PagerDuty notification channel as I outlined earlier.

5.1 Add PagerDuty Integration
Go to Alerting > Contact Point.
Add Contact Point.
Name it PagerDuty Alerts.
Select PagerDuty as the type.
Enter your PagerDuty Integration Key.
Click Save.
5.2 Create a High CPU Usage Alert
Go to Alerting > Alert Rules.
Click + Create Alert Rule.
Name it High CPU Usage Alert.
Add query:
100 - (avg by (instance) (rate(node_cpu_seconds_total{mode="idle"}[5m])) * 100)
Set condition:
When last value is above 90
For duration: 1 minute
2. Under Notifications, select PagerDuty Alerts.

3. Click Save Alert Rule.

Step 6: Testing Alerts
Go to Alerting > Alert Rules.
Click Test Rule.
If CPU usage exceeds 90%, an alert will trigger.
Check PagerDuty for incident creation.
